        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "tests/test_requirement_intake.py, test_missing_configuration_is_a_named_error: `create = unittest.mock.Mock()` is never patched into `ri.managed_task.create_task`, yet `create.assert_not_called()` is asserted. The spec scenario 'Missing or ambiguous routing input ... creates nothing' is therefore only covered by the raised error. The scenario's 'Backlog label absent' case also has no test.",
                  "id": "vacuous-missing-config-test",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The missing-configuration test asserts `create.assert_not_called()` on a mock that is never wired into materialize_handoff, so that assertion proves nothing about the 'creates nothing' scenario."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/requirement_intake.py materialize_handoff: the new `config = managed_task.authoring_config(root)` / `resolve_child_routing(...)` block is placed before `requirement_target_lifecycle.require_local_target_support(...)`. Previously `authoring_config` was called after the target-support check.",
                  "id": "routing-check-ordering-before-target-support",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "`managed_task.authoring_config` and `resolve_child_routing` now run before the target-lifecycle support check, so a project without `[development_backlog]` configuration now fails with 'child routing input missing' instead of the more specific target-support error. This is a minor change in error pr"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "11ede544a85e2d343bb6df06524270d511df7af2f5065b57967efd6b43367db3"
            },
            "spec-fidelity": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/requirement_intake.py verify_child_routing error text says \"Correct the project label on {child_ref} manually (or close it and retry)\". Candidate search in materialize_handoff (line ~749) queries `issues?state=all` and reuses the matching handoff-marker child. A closed child therefore becomes the reused candidate and verify_child_routing then raises \"child ... is not open\". design.md decision 4 has the same guidance and doesn't account for this.",
                  "id": "close-and-retry-guidance-dead-end",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The mislabeled-child repair guidance says to \"close it and retry\". The retry would still find the closed child and reject it, so that path can't succeed."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "verify_child_routing: `if issue.get(\"state\") != \"open\": raise ...`. Spec scenarios for read-back mismatch list only project label, type:internal-change and the back-reference.",
                  "id": "open-state-check-not-in-spec",
                  "severity": "advisory",
